---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

// The facts on this page are read from openIE-dev/rce at this commit
// (scripts/install.sh, .github/workflows/release.yml, docs/DEPLOY.md, ide/README.md).
const commit = '0c015c43';
const repo = 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce';
const releases = `${repo}/releases`;
const platforms = [
  { name: 'linux-x86_64', what: 'Linux on 64-bit Intel and AMD processors' },
  { name: 'linux-aarch64', what: 'Linux on 64-bit Arm' },
  { name: 'macos-aarch64', what: 'macOS on Apple silicon' },
  { name: 'windows-x86_64', what: 'Windows on 64-bit Intel and AMD processors' },
  { name: 'wasm32-wasip1', what: 'WebAssembly for the WebAssembly System Interface (WASI), for a WASI runtime such as Wasmtime; the archive holds rce.wasm' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Download RCE"
  description="Install the RCE checker rce from the release of every main commit that passed CI, run it from the container image, deploy a program with the guide, build it from source, or build the RCE IDE from source."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">research.openie.dev / rce</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">Download RCE</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      RCE (the Reality Code Engine) is a language in which a program is written once as a checked state machine and code in other languages is generated from it.
      Its reference checker, <code>rce</code>, admits a program or names the rule it breaks, runs it, emits it as Rust, Python, JavaScript or Scala, and runs it as a service on the host runtime.
      All of it is public source in <a href={repo} class="text-brand-cyan">openIE-dev/rce</a>: the specification, the Lean proofs, the checker, the host runtime, <code>rce db</code>, the apps, the standard library and the integrated development environment (IDE).
      The research behind it is in <a href="/papers/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">the RCE paper</a>.
      What this page states was read from openIE-dev/rce at commit <code>{commit}</code>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Try it in the browser</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The <a href="https://openie-dev.github.io/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">RCE playground</a> runs the reference checker, compiled to WebAssembly, in your browser.
      Type a program and see whether it is accepted, which rule it breaks, and the trace of each <code>example</code>. Nothing is installed and nothing is sent to a server.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Install with one command</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      On Linux, macOS or Windows (in a Git Bash or MSYS2 shell):
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-3 p-3 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-xs"><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openIE-dev/rce/main/scripts/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The script downloads the archive for your platform from the release <code>rce-latest</code>, checks it against the release's <code>SHA256SUMS</code> (SHA-256 is the Secure Hash Algorithm with a 256-bit digest) and installs nothing if the hash differs.
      It installs <code>rce</code> into <code>~/.local/bin</code> (set <code>RCE_INSTALL_DIR</code> to choose another directory) and runs <code>rce --version</code>, which prints the commit the binary was built from.
      To pin one commit, pass its first 12 hexadecimal digits: <code>sh install.sh 0c015c431031</code>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Releases</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Every commit of <code>main</code> that passes continuous integration (CI) is released, named by its commit and never by a typed version:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><code>rce-&lt;commit&gt;</code>, where <code>&lt;commit&gt;</code> is the first 12 hexadecimal digits of the commit; the 30 newest are kept, for pinning.</li>
      <li><code>rce-latest</code>, which points at the newest of them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Each release holds <code>rce-&lt;platform&gt;.tar.gz</code> for five platforms and one <code>SHA256SUMS</code> file. Each archive holds the binary and the license files. All releases: <a href={releases} class="text-brand-cyan">github.com/openIE-dev/rce/releases</a>.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 list-none p-0 m-0">
      {platforms.map((p) => (
        <li class="glass-card p-5">
          <a href={`${releases}/download/rce-latest/rce-${p.name}.tar.gz`} class="font-mono text-sm text-brand-cyan break-all">rce-{p.name}.tar.gz</a>
          <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">{p.what}.</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">To check an archive by hand, download it and <code>SHA256SUMS</code> into one folder, then:</p>
    <pre class="mt-2 p-3 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-xs"><code>sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing     # Linux
shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing # macOS
tar xzf rce-linux-x86_64.tar.gz &amp;&amp; ./rce/rce --version</code></pre>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Container image</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The same release builds a public container image, <code>ghcr.io/openie-dev/rce</code>, tagged <code>latest</code> and with the full commit hash for pinning. It runs <code>rce</code> as an unprivileged user, with the working directory <code>/srv</code> and the volume <code>/data</code>.
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-3 p-3 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-xs"><code>docker run --rm ghcr.io/openie-dev/rce:latest --version</code></pre>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Run a program in production</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/DEPLOY.md`} class="text-brand-cyan">docs/DEPLOY.md</a> runs an HTTP notes service as an RCE program on the host runtime: check it, serve it from the container or the installed binary, stop and restart it, back up and replay its log, and change the program.
      The program's durable log is the only thing to keep: the state is always the replay of the log.
      A log is bound to the program that wrote it (rule HC-27): beside the log the host keeps the program's module hash, and <code>rce host run</code>, <code>serve</code> and <code>replay</code> refuse a program whose hash differs, before the log is opened.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Build from source</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The checker is <code>spec/checker</code> of <a href={repo} class="text-brand-cyan">openIE-dev/rce</a>, built with the Rust toolchain pinned in <code>spec/checker/rust-toolchain.toml</code>:
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-3 p-3 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-xs"><code>git clone https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce
cd rce/spec/checker
cargo build --release --bin rce
./target/release/rce --version</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The repository's README lists the other checks: the specification check (<code>rce-spec-check</code>), the tests, the Lean proofs and the conformance suite.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">The RCE IDE</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The RCE IDE bundles the editor (<code>rce-ide</code>), the checker, a language server (<code>rce-lsp</code>) and a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for coding agents (<code>rce-mcp</code>).
      Its source is <a href={`${repo}/tree/main/ide`} class="text-brand-cyan">ide/</a> in openIE-dev/rce, built against the checker of the same commit:
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-3 p-3 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-xs"><code>cd rce/ide
cargo build --release -p rce-ide -p rce-mcp</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The earlier IDE releases, v0.1.0 to v0.1.3, are on the <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-ide/releases" class="text-brand-cyan">releases page of openIE-dev/rce-ide</a>, with their own <code>SHA256SUMS</code>. They predate the move of the IDE into openIE-dev/rce and are not rebuilt; for an IDE at a current commit, build it from <code>ide/</code>.
      The repositories openIE-dev/rce-ide, rce-book, rce-stdlib, rce-examples, rce-conformance and tree-sitter-rce now point to directories of openIE-dev/rce.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">License</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The source in openIE-dev/rce is licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option. Copyright (c) 2026 Open Interface Engineering, Inc (OpenIE).
      Third-party notices for the IDE are in <code>ide/release/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt</code>.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/rce/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10">Read the RCE paper</a>
      <a href="/rce/spec/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10">RCE spec</a>
      <a href="/faq/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white">FAQ</a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white">Catalog</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
